{
  "info": {
    "name": "Fuel Route Optimizer",
    "description": "POST /api/v1/routes/plan — given a start and destination, returns the route (GeoJSON) and the minimum-cost fuel stops for a 10 MPG / 500-mile-range / 50-gallon-tank vehicle, using the supplied CSV prices. Stations are enriched (real per-station coordinates, not city-center approximations) across ten states: AL, CA, FL, GA, LA, MS, NM, NV, OK, TX. Set the `base_url` collection variable (default http://localhost:8000). Each request has Postman tests asserting the expected status/code.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Happy paths",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Coordinate/Coordinate — OKC to Albuquerque",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(\"Fuel plan is feasible\", function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json().fuel.feasible).to.eql(true); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"start\": {\n    \"latitude\": 35.473,\n    \"longitude\": -97.5171\n  },\n  \"destination\": {\n    \"latitude\": 35.0841,\n    \"longitude\": -106.651\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/routes/plan",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "routes",
                "plan"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Both locations supplied as coordinates -> zero geocoding calls, exactly one routing call on a cache miss. Expected: 200 OK. route.distance_miles ~544.7 (a real ~545-mile I-40 drive, which exceeds the 500-mile max range), fuel.feasible=true, exactly one real fuel stop from the supplied CSV (a real station near Amarillo, TX), fuel.total_gallons_purchased and fuel.total_cost both > 0. Observed: 1 stop (CEFCO #2005, Amarillo TX @ $2.869), total_cost ≈ 12.82."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Cached repeat — resend Request 1",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "pm.test(\"Fuel plan is feasible\", function () { pm.expect(pm.response.json().fuel.feasible).to.eql(true); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"start\": {\n    \"latitude\": 35.473,\n    \"longitude\": -97.5171\n  },\n  \"destination\": {\n    \"latitude\": 35.0841,\n    \"longitude\": -106.651\n  }\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/routes/plan",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "routes",
                "plan"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Identical body to Request 1 — send this AFTER Request 1 has already succeeded once. Expected: 200 OK with the exact same route/fuel/stops as Request 1, but served from the DB-backed RouteCacheEntry — no second OSRM call is made. Observable from the server side via a noticeably faster response and an unchanged RouteCacheEntry row count; not distinguishable from the HTTP response alone, which is the point — caching is transparent to the client."
          }
        },
